    "learn_founder_story": {
      "type": "learn-founder-story",
      "name": "Learn founder story",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "HOW BRISA STARTED.",
        "intro": "<p>I was at work trying to talk the boys off the vapes. I've always hated them. Watching mates I care about smoke chemicals nobody can pronounce never sat right with me.</p>",
        "quote": "It's not the nicotine, mate. It's the hand-to-mouth. Every time I try to stop, that's what pulls me back.",
        "body": "<p>That stuck. I went home, did the research, called Kaiden. We bought every product we could find, tested them all, and knew what was missing and what to produce.</p><p>They all missed the same things. Felt cheap in your hand. Looked out of place pulling out at the pub or on a worksite, or replaced bad stuff with more bad stuff. Nothing anyone actually wanted.</p><p>So we built our own option. Same motion. Same draw. Same moment. No chemicals, no nicotine, no vapour. Built solid. Looks the part. Flavours people actually know, with every aspect in mind.</p><p>Something Aussies are happy to be seen with.</p><p>That's Brisa. Still the two of us behind it.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/founders.jpg",
        "signature": "— SAM & KAIDEN, CO-FOUNDERS",
        "max_width": 520,
        "background": "#ffffff",
        "padding_top": 40,
        "padding_bottom": 24
      }
    },
    "learn_questions": {
      "type": "learn-questions",
      "blocks": {
        "question_loop": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "label": "01 - THE LOOP",
            "title": "It's not a choice anymore. It's a loop.",
            "text": "<p>Most people don't realise how much the vape starts running their day. It becomes the thing you reach for when you wake up, after food, in the car, at work, when you're stressed, when you're bored, every time you need a break. The vape starts running your schedule before you notice.</p>",
            "quote": "If you can put it down whenever you want, why is it always in your hand?"
          }
        },
        "question_steal": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "label": "02 - THE STEAL",
            "title": "It's not just your lungs. It's your sleep, your mood, your training.",
            "text": "<p>Vaping feels like it calms you down, but nicotine is still a stimulant. It's linked to trouble falling asleep, waking through the night, poorer recovery, and feeling more tired the next day. So it's not just stealing your breath — it's stealing your energy.</p>",
            "quote": "How much of your energy, sleep and performance is it quietly stealing every day?"
          }
        },
        "question_bill": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "label": "03 - THE BILL",
            "title": "It's a weekly bill dressed up as a small expense.",
            "text": "<p>Disposables, pods, coils, juice — none of it feels like much in the moment. But over months and years, it adds up fast. The worst part? You're not paying for something that builds your life. You're paying to stay stuck.</p>",
            "quote": "How much has this habit already cost you, and what could that money have built instead?"
          }
        },
        "question_hide": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "label": "04 - THE HIDE",
            "title": "It starts to make people feel weak.",
            "text": "<p>Most people don't want to be the person ducking off for a hit, hiding it from family, or stressing when the vape's dead. It slowly becomes something you rely on — then something you're embarrassed by.</p>",
            "quote": "Why does it feel so good to imagine not needing it anymore?"
          }
        },
        "question_future": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "label": "05 - THE FUTURE",
            "title": "We don't know what 40 years of this looks like yet.",
            "text": "<p>One vape can carry as much nicotine as 50 cigarettes. Cigarettes had friction — lighters, smell, a clear finish. Vapes removed all of it. Easier to hide, easier to hit constantly, and more frequent than nicotine has ever been in human history.</p>",
            "quote": "What are lifelong vapers going to look like after decades of this?"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "question_loop",
